  ## 4. RECOMMENDATIONS
     · 4.1 RANKED, each with Why (n, $, the part it cites), Class, Touches and the Decision needed from the
       operator; a "Still open from last week" table at the foot. Never a knob, a study toggle, a resting
       take-profit or a new order rule.
     · 4.2 THE QQQ CASH SIZE TABLE (standing, every Saturday UNTIL the cash start 2026-12-07; the last run is
       Saturday 12-05). If this Saturday is on or after 2026-12-07, skip it and do not mention it. Otherwise take
       every QQQ trade in ~/reviews/trades/*.csv dated 2026-10-26 through this Friday (OTV4TEST rows out) and
       re-size each entry under two schemes, with the per-trade cap = the ramp max (OT_BREAKOUT_BUDGET_USD; OT_ORB_BUDGET_USD before OTV5 r125) in both.
       The ramp max is read only by Breakout's _size_geometry, so it binds Breakout's rows only (dormant since OTV5
       r110; no Breakout row after 2026-11-13); every other setup sizes on the base alone:
         A) base OT_RISK_USD $250, ramp max $500        B) base OT_RISK_USD $500, ramp max $750
       The rule is OTV5 risk/risk_manager.py size_for, as the code runs it today. The grade multiplier is 1.0, and
       OT_SIZE_ON_RISK is off by default, so there is no deploy cap and no risk-to-stop denominator.
       Hunt, Runaway, PARK and OGAP take _size_budget: floor(base / (entry x 100)) (OGAP passes the base as its own
       budget, OTV5 r131, on the mark, r136). Under 1 contract the trade is REFUSED
       (insufficient_capital), never rounded up to 1.
       Breakout takes _size_geometry, which ramps. by_budget = floor(ramp max / (entry x 100)); under 1 the trade
       is REFUSED (the ramp-max refusal). Otherwise contracts = min(by_risk, by_budget), where:
         by_risk = max(1, floor(base / ((entry - stop premium) x 100))) when 0 < stop premium < entry,
                   else the geometry count max(1, floor(width / distance))
         width = orb_range_high - orb_range_low, distance = |underlying_entry - underlying_stop|
       A stop wider than the range (distance > width) sizes min(by_risk, by_budget) when there is a usable stop
       premium, and 1 contract without one. Every input comes from the warehouse trade row (load_trades).
       Scale each kept trade's P&L and fee by new contracts / actual contracts.
       Report, per scheme and per setup (Hunt, Runaway, PARK, OGAP, and Breakout's rows to 2026-11-13): entries traded vs refused, contracts
       min/median/max, the re-sized P&L with fees beside it (never in it), EV a trade with a day-bootstrap 95%
       interval, the worst day, and the largest single-trade loss. Lead with each scheme's window EV and its
       interval. A Breakout trade with neither a usable stop premium nor width and distance goes to NOT MEASURED
       by trade_id. REPORT ONLY: the operator sets the size, the ramp and the cap themselves when they activate
       cash. It is not a study (never in WEEKEND_STUDIES.md), and it sits in section 4 as a reference table, never an R-item.
     · 4.3 THE 12-04 CASH-TEST READINESS CHECKLIST (every Saturday brief dated on or before 2026-12-04; QQQ only,
       the normal budget, one RTH session, a careful log review after). Each item DONE (with evidence), OPEN, or
       WAITING ON THE OPERATOR: (1) OT_DAILY_LOSS_LIMIT confirmed for the QQQ box: the start-up banner's
       catastrophic_loss_cap= value from the QQQ box's bot.log (grep -m1 -F, the line only) beside OTV5 config.py's
       default, never from .env or a unit's Environment; the operator confirms it; (2) the tastytrade auto-exercise
       cut-off for an in-the-money long option held into the close, against the fleet's 15:40 / 15:50 / 15:55 end of
       day, and whether any position was open after 15:50 this week; the operator confirms the broker's rule;
       (3) the Hunt decision and (4) the OGAP decision, from 2A; (5) the test-day log checklist (every entry's
       ladder walk and fill, every exit's ladder, refusals and caps, feed episodes, the loss-limit state, order
       rejects, the 15:50/15:55 close, the broker's fills against the bot's record), written once, then carried.
