       half day, the 13:00 ET close, a non-trading day: no entries, data only); the Fed and CPI from the bot's own economic-calendar source (OTV5
       config.FOREX_FACTORY_URL, current week only; its ff_calendar_nextweek.json sibling when it answers, else NOT
       MEASURED with the reason); earnings on our symbols: earnings.expected-report-date from the Friday's S3
       raw/market_metrics/dt=<Fri>/sym=<SYM>/ (TastyTrade), listed when it falls next week.
     · 4.5 THE SUNDAY WORK LIST, LAST: every item for a yes (from 4.1, 3B, 3C, 2B), one line each: id, what lands,
       its gate, its size, DELICATE (the live order path, entries, exits, sizing, a box service, anything that
       trades) or ROUTINE (control-only tools, docs, studies, tests); DELICATE first. The brief ENDS with it.
  Put an INDEX on top (one headline line per part, 1A..4) and a NOT MEASURED list at the foot, after the Sunday
  work list.

THE RULES (the spec explains each one):
  · Plain language. Say "they/them" for the operator. Say n every time. Edge is judged over the horizon, never on
    one day.
  · Report only setups that closed a trade or wrote a shadow row in the week. Retired strategies are not named,
    listed or scored anywhere except as code to remove in 3C; a setup that no longer trades is the one unnamed
    history line in the epoch tables.
  · No non-events. Leave out what did not happen or did not change. End each part with one
    "Checked, nothing to report:" line naming what came back clean.
  · Filter the OTV4TEST fleet's rows out of every warehouse measurement with
    OTV5 tests/warehouse_source.mainline(). 1A's EXCLUDED line names what it dropped, every week.
  · Fees are reported beside P&L and never inside EV.
  · A 13:00 half day is a NON-TRADING day by the operator's ruling (2026-11-22: "Yes, just treat them as bank
    holidays. No trading."; OTV5 r145 opens nothing, the boxes record data only; 2026-11-27, 2026-12-24). It is never
    a session (weekly_facts, cash_books and runaway_watch all leave it out), zero trades on it is never a defect, a
    non-event or a study, and a trade that opened on one IS a defect (OTV5 HALF.1): weekly_facts names it on a DEFECT
    line, and 3A reports it.
  · Market data is TastyTrade's (S3); never yfinance here.
  · Never state what you did not measure (§0, §0.1). A measurement that could not be taken goes
    in NOT MEASURED, by name, with the reason (§0.5).
  · Use /home/ubuntu/day_trader_pro/venv/bin/python for every Python tool, never a bare python3.
  · The R suite runs OTV5's tools: /home/ubuntu/OTV5/tests/{r_ledger,stop_sweep,exit_replay,edge_scan}.py.
    The menu's _r_tool still points at the frozen otv4 tree. Do not use it.

THE BOXES: READ-ONLY, AND NO CREDENTIALS, EVER.
  · Reads only: no restart, bake, pull, reconcile, purge, delete or edit. SQLite with mode=ro.
  · Never print an environment or a unit: no `systemctl show` without a property filter, no
    `systemctl cat`, `env`, /proc/*/environ, .env, ~/.flash_creds or bootstrap. Service state
    comes from `systemctl is-active <unit>` only. botlog_scan redacts on the box. Keep it that way.
  · Wake and stop the fleet ONLY with wake_and_bake (study_dispatch.py powers only the boxes it claims). The fleet count comes from the instance map:
      WAKE   cd /home/ubuntu/day_trader_pro && ./venv/bin/python wake_and_bake.py --wake-only --yes
      CLOSE  cd /home/ubuntu/day_trader_pro && ./venv/bin/python wake_and_bake.py --shutdown-only --yes
    Do the box reads (3A, and 4.3's banner line) right after the wake. Friday night's study dispatch has finished and
    stopped its boxes (2B); only when 2B's FALLBACK 1 applies, START the study dispatch now.
    If you started it, do NOT CLOSE while it runs: CLOSE would stop the boxes running studies. It stops the boxes
    it does not use and the ones it finishes with; its own power calls go through ec2ops, the logged chokepoint.
    At the end: run `study_dispatch.py wait` (if you started one), then
    `./venv/bin/python tools/study_dispatch.py cleanup` (only its own claimed boxes; run it either way), then CLOSE. YOU MUST CLOSE THE FLEET BEFORE YOU FINISH,
    INCLUDING ON FAILURE. Then quote the "N/N reached 'stopped'" line. If you cannot quote it, say so at
    the top of NOT MEASURED.
  · Never wake during 09:30-16:00 ET. If you are run by hand then, the box reads are NOT MEASURED.

YOU LAND NOTHING AND YOU SEND NOTHING. No git commit, no push, no tools/deploy.sh, no land.sh,
no Telegram or pager (§17: the alert path is for emergencies, and a weekly report is not one).
The operator approves every land. You write ONE markdown file at BRIEF, keep your working files
in WORK, update the study queue's item status (2B), and stop. Study folders go under
~/reviews/studies/, as the queue says.

TIME: you have until the DEADLINE below (about 07:30 ET). Run the long jobs (the checker sweep,
the exit replay, the study dispatch) in the background with nohup, a timeout and an rc line,
one heavy job at a time through `flock /tmp/claude-heavy.lock env HEAVY_MAX=2500M /home/ubuntu/bin/heavy`, and
write parts as their inputs arrive. A brief with five parts done and five in NOT MEASURED is better than no file at all.

Lead each part with what changed. The operator reads it with their morning coffee.
